# Review Map: LLM settings.
# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in ONE provider's key.
# Real environment variables override values in `.env`.
# Without any key, Review Map still works with a heuristic (low-confidence) parser.
#
# Provider choice: REVIEW_MAP_LLM_PROVIDER if set, else `llm.provider` in
# .reviewmap.yml, else the first provider whose key is set, in this order:
# Groq, Gemini, Anthropic, OpenAI. (Ollama is used only when chosen explicitly.)

# --- Default: Groq (free tier, OpenAI-compatible) ---------------------------
# Get a key at https://console.groq.com/keys
REVIEW_MAP_LLM_PROVIDER=groq
REVIEW_MAP_LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- Free fallback: Google Gemini (OpenAI-compatible endpoint) ---------------
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# To use it, comment out the Groq lines above (or leave GROQ_API_KEY out and
# remove REVIEW_MAP_LLM_PROVIDER so auto-detection picks Gemini).
# REVIEW_MAP_LLM_PROVIDER=gemini
# REVIEW_MAP_LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Anthropic (official SDK) ------------------------------------------------
# REVIEW_MAP_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# REVIEW_MAP_LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- OpenAI ------------------------------------------------------------------
# REVIEW_MAP_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# REVIEW_MAP_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Ollama (local, free, offline; run `ollama serve` first) ----------------
# REVIEW_MAP_LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# REVIEW_MAP_LLM_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
# REVIEW_MAP_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (proxy, self-hosted server):
# REVIEW_MAP_LLM_BASE_URL=
# Where LLM answers are cached (default: ~/.cache/review-map/llm):
# REVIEW_MAP_CACHE_DIR=

# --- GitHub (optional for public reads; required to post PR comments) --------
# Without a token, `review-map pr` works on public repos at 60 API requests an
# hour. A token raises that to 5,000 and lets you read private repos.
# Create a fine-grained token at https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# (public repos: no extra permissions; private: read-only Contents and Pull requests).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Where `review-map pr` keeps repo clones (default: ~/.cache/review-map/repos):
# REVIEW_MAP_REPO_CACHE_DIR=
